-- title:
--   Sections along base change by Spec of a surjection
-- statement:
--   Let $\varphi : A \to A'$ be a morphism of commutative rings whose underlying ring homomorphism is surjective, let $Y, Y'$ be schemes, and let $g : Y' \to Y$, $i_Y : Y \to \operatorname{Spec} A$, $i_{Y'} : Y' \to \operatorname{Spec} A'$ be morphisms such that the square with sides $g$, $i_{Y'}$ and $i_Y$, $\operatorname{Spec}\varphi$ is a pullback square, so $g$ followed by $i_Y$ equals $i_{Y'}$ followed by $\operatorname{Spec}\varphi$ and $Y'$ realises $Y \times_{\operatorname{Spec} A} \operatorname{Spec} A'$. Let $W$ be an open subscheme-datum of $Y$ (an element of `Y.Opens`) which is an affine open. The conclusion has two parts: first, the ring homomorphism $g^{\sharp}_W : \Gamma(Y, W) \to \Gamma(Y', g^{-1}W)$ induced by $g$ on sections over $W$ is surjective; second, its kernel is the ideal of $\Gamma(Y, W)$ generated by the image of $\ker\varphi$ under the structure homomorphism $A \to \Gamma(Y, W)$, spelled as the inverse of the canonical isomorphism $A \cong \Gamma(\operatorname{Spec} A, \top)$ followed by the restriction map $i_Y^{\sharp}$ from $\top$ to $W$. Thus $\Gamma(Y', g^{-1}W) = \Gamma(Y, W)/(\ker\varphi)\Gamma(Y, W)$.
--
--   This is the affine-local description of a base change by a closed immersion of affine base schemes: on an affine open $W$ of $Y$ the ring of sections of the fibre product is the quotient of $\Gamma(Y,W)$ by the extended ideal, equivalently $\Gamma(Y,W) \otimes_A A'$. It is used in the construction of modules over the truncations $\operatorname{Spec}(R/I^{n})$ of an adic base, where the transition maps of the resulting system of rings of sections are surjective with kernel the extension of the corresponding ideal.
